stency-Driven Learning for AI-Generated Image Detection with Vision-Language Large Models | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-37023-5_10)\nciteturn207view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn206view2\",\"lineno\":10}); Total lines: 436\nL0: Account\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Menu】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Find a journal】 【2†Publish with us†www.springernature.com】 【3†Track your research†link.springernature.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【4†Search】\nL7: \nL8: 【5†Saved research】\nL9: \nL10: 【6†Cart†order.springer.com】\nL11: # UC-VLM: Consistency-Driven Learning for AI-Generated Image Detection with Vision-Language Large Models\nL12: \nL13:   * Conference paper\nL14:   * First Online: 11 September 2026\nL15: \nL16:   * pp 164–183\nL17:   * 【7†Cite this conference paper】\nL18: \nL19: 【8†Save conference paper】\nL20: \nL21: 【5†View saved research】\nL22: \nL23: 【9†Computer Vision – ECCV 2026】 (ECCV 2026)\nL24:   * 【10†Lei Tan】  【11†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-2766-681X†orcid.org】^{【12†13】},\nL25:   * 【13†Shuwei Li】  【14†ORCID: orcid.org/0009-0002-0148-7351†orcid.org】^{【12†13】},\nL26:   * 【15†Mohan Kankanhalli】  【16†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-4846-2015†orcid.org】^{【12†13】} &\nL27:   * …\nL28:   * 【17†Robby T. Tan】  【18†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0001-7532-6919†orcid.org】^{【12†13】}\nL29: Show authors\nL30: \nL31: Part of the book series: 【19†Lecture Notes in Computer Science】 ((LNCS,volume 17069))\nL32: \nL33: Included in the following conference series:\nL34:   * 【20†European Conference on Computer Vision】\nL35: \nL36:   * 1436 Accesses\nL37: \nL38:   * 1 【21†Altmetric†link.altmetric.com】\nL39: ## Abstract\nL40: Vision-Language Large Models (VLLMs) are promising for AI-generated image (AIGI) detection because they can produce both a prediction and a natural-language output. However, most existing VLLM-based detectors primarily fine-tune the language side while giving limited attention to low-level visual forensic cues. They also often depend on manually crafted prompts or human-annotated rationales, which limits scalability.\nL41: We present UC-VLM, a unified multi-stage framework for AIGI detection that relies solely on binary supervision. UC-VLM first identifies effective instruction variants automatically. It then reuses the same binary label within a multi-stage training framework: (i) a visual discrimination objective that strengthens sensitivity to non-semantic forensic cues, and (ii) a label-conditioned generation objective that uses the binary label to supervise textual outputs.\nL42: This design turns weak binary supervision into a shared supervision signal for both the visual pathway and the language output. Our key novelty is a unified multi-stage binary-supervised framework that consistently reuses the same authenticity labels for visual adaptation and label-conditioned text generation, while leveraging automatically optimized instructions to reduce prompt sensitivity without requiring human-written rationales or hand-crafted prompts.\nL43: Experiments show that UC-VLM achieves 96.1% average accuracy on GenImage, exceeding the strongest prior result by 4.6%, and obtains 69.6%/77.9% accuracy on Chameleon under ProGAN/SDV1.4 training, surpassing the best baseline by 11.2%/15.3%, respectively.\nL44: This is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\nL45: ## Access this chapter\nL46: \nL47: Log in via an institution\nL48: \nL49: ## Subscribe and save\nL50: \nL51: Springer+\nL52: \nL53: from $39.99 /Month\nL54: \nL55:   * Starting from 10 chapters or articles per month\nL56:   * Access and download chapters and articles from more than 300k books and 2,500 journals\nL57:   * Cancel anytime\nL58: 【22†View plans】\nL59: ## Buy Now\nL60: \nL61: Chapter\nL62: \nL63: \nL64: USD 29.95\nL65: \nL66:     Price excludes VAT (USA)\nL67: \nL68: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL69: \nL70:   * Available as PDF\nL71:   * Read on any device\nL